### Steps to reproduce the behaviour

When performing consecutive searches, the results from the previous search remain visible in the main table alongside the new results. This appears to be a race condition in the asynchronous updateSearchMatches logic within MainTableDataModel

1. Open a library with multiple entries.
2. Search for a term that matches "Entry A".
3. Immediately search for a term that matches "Entry B".
4. Observe that both "Entry A" and "Entry B" are visible in the table.

I have verified this bug using the following JUnit 5 test case added to MainTableDataModelTest.java. This test fails with an AssertionFailedError because the matching count is 2 instead of 1.

@Test
